-- title:
--   Mod p parabolic eigenclass gives maximal ideal of T₂(N)
-- statement:
--   Let $N\ge 1$ and let $S\subseteq\mathbb N$ be a set containing every prime divisor of $N$. Let $p$ be a prime, let $Q$ be a predicate on natural numbers and let $a:\mathbb N\to\mathbb Z$ be any function. Let $x$ lie in [`ModularCurve.Period.parabolicHoms ℤ (Gamma0 N) ℤ`](def/ModularCurve_PeriodMap.html#L62), i.e. $x$ is an additive homomorphism from $\Gamma_0(N)$ (written additively) to $\mathbb Z$ that vanishes on every $\gamma$ with $\operatorname{tr}(\gamma)^2=4$. Assume that the reduction of $x$ modulo $p$, that is $\mathbb Z\to\mathbb Z/p$ composed after $x$, is nonzero, and that for every prime $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid N$ and $Q(\ell)$ the homomorphism $\mathrm{T}_\ell x-a(\ell)\,x$ reduces to $0$ modulo $p$, where $\mathrm{T}_\ell=$ [`HeckeEis.heckeOperatorHom N ℓ ℤ`](def/Gamma0HeckeOperatorHom.html#L285) is pullback along `heckeConj N ℓ` from $\Gamma_0(N)$ to the subgroup `heckeUpper N ℓ`, followed by corestriction (transfer) back to $\Gamma_0(N)$. Then the weight-two Hecke algebra [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb C}S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the operators `heckeTLin 2` at primes $\ell\nmid N$, $\ell\notin S$ together with the `heckeULin 2` at primes $q\mid N$, $q\notin S$ (of which, by the hypothesis on $S$, there are none), admits a maximal ideal $\mathfrak m$ containing $p$ and containing $\mathrm{T}_\ell-a(\ell)$ for every prime $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid N$ and $Q(\ell)$.
--
--   This is the cohomology-to-Hecke-algebra direction of the Eichler–Shimura dictionary modulo $p$ in weight two: a system of Hecke eigenvalues realised modulo $p$ in the integral parabolic cohomology of $\Gamma_0(N)$ is realised by a maximal ideal of residue characteristic $p$ in the anemic weight-two Hecke algebra. It feeds the level-raising step, being used in [`WeierstrassCurve.exists_ideal_heckeAlgebra_mul_two_of_ideal_heckeAlgebra_two_or_succ`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.exists_ideal_heckeAlgebra_mul_two_of_ideal_heckeAlgebra_two_or_succ).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_Period_exists_ideal_heckeAlgebra_two_of_int_modp_eigenclass.lean

